id: automation/yawn.bot.feedback-loop
title: "yawn.bot feedback loop"
kind: automation-gate
status: active
updated: 2026-09-07

purpose: >
  Define how yawn.bot turns feedback into a thesis, weighs risk, and decides
  whether a contribution is ready to be committed; and, since 2026-09-07, how
  an interface feedback packet filed inside YAWN.bot closes on its own into
  one email to the owner.

closed_loop:
  ruled_by: "Dave, 2026-09-07 (voice): after I submit the feedback, all I do is wait for an email"
  implementation: "https://github.com/yawn-ai/yawn.bot — YAWNS/Observations/YAWN_DAVE_APERTURE_VIEW_AND_FEEDBACK_AUTONOMY_2026_09_07.yawn"
  stages:
    - id: filed
      surface: "yawn.bot header feedback control (select a surface, say what is wrong, file)"
      record: "yawn.feedback_event.v1 at yawn.bot/feedback, routed to yawn.bot/the-yawn-company/target-inspector-yawn"
      receipt: "Open in Feedback (the packet) · Work order (the packet with its work order open) · build lane"
    - id: proposed
      switch: propose
      effect: "one build proposal per packet, id derived from owner and packet; a replayed save reports the same run"
    - id: granted
      switch: approve
      effect: "the exact revision is granted; the paired local worker claims, builds, verifies, opens a pull request"
    - id: released
      switch: release
      effect: "the merge plane takes automatic_when_green for the exact proven head when every required check and coherence axis is green"
    - id: emailed
      recipient: "dave@yawn.ai (the owner of the yawn.bot)"
      subject_shape: "Fixed: <title> — yawn.bot<route>"
      body: "the feedback text, a link to the packet's work order, the live route, the pull request"
  switches:
    location: "owner coding state, Build YAWN panel → Feedback autonomy"
    default: "on for the owner who ruled it; each switch separately revocable"
  boundary:
    - "a lane that cannot open (disabled, unavailable, off) is named on the receipt; the packet is never lost"
    - "release never widens the worker sandbox, spends, or accepts a head the merge plane would refuse"
    - "the aperture of a coordinate changes what renders (route-carried view), never truth or permission"

loop:
  - collect feedback and repo signals
  - parse each signal into a node
  - look for repeated lacunae
  - form a clear thesis
  - weigh risks and proof
  - choose the smallest bounded change
  - route commit-ready work to private draft PR staging
  - notify Dave when a private draft PR exists
  - preserve human review and replay outcome

signal_strength:
  none: "no external issue, pull request, email, or feedback signal"
  single_signal: "one signal with unclear pattern"
  pattern_forming: "two or more related signals, or one high-severity proof-backed issue"
  thesis_ready: "a recurring lacuna can be stated as a clear, testable thesis"
  commit_ready: "the thesis, risk review, proof check, rollback path, and authority state are all explicit"
  draft_pr_opened: "a private draft PR exists in the staging repository"
  human_review: "a human is reviewing meaning, risk, and promotion"
  accepted: "a human accepted the pattern or promoted a sanitized version"
  revised: "the pattern needs another bounded pass"
  rejected: "the pattern should not be promoted"
  stale: "the pattern or PR no longer has current evidence"

thesis_shape:
  claim: "what enough feedback appears to show"
  affected_node: "where the change belongs"
  proposed_move: "the smallest repo change that could reduce the lacuna"
  proof: "what would show the change helped"
  dissent: "what feedback or risk argues against the move"

risk_review:
  - low-quality feedback may look like a pattern before it is one
  - the bot may overfit to the loudest signal
  - a helpful change may make first-use onboarding harder
  - private feedback may include personal data
  - automation may appear to have authority it does not have
  - commits may create maintenance burden or obscure human intent

commit_gate:
  required_before_commit:
    - signal strength is thesis_ready or commit_ready
    - affected node is named
    - smallest bounded file change is named
    - proof check is named
    - risk review includes dissent or uncertainty
    - rollback path is named
    - core-loop.yawn draft PR authorization or explicit current human authorization is present
  default_commit_target: "branch or draft pull request, not direct main"
  private_staging_target: "yawn-ai/yawn-bot-staging"
  main_branch_rule: "main branch updates require explicit human authorization until a future policy changes this"
  notification_target: "dave@yawn.ai through automation/yawn.bot.pr-notification.yawn"

blocked_before_private_pr:
  - missing exact bounded diff
  - missing deterministic validation
  - missing rollback path
  - missing privacy review
  - missing rate budget
  - public-only promotion request without Dave approval

daily_output:
  - signal strength
  - thesis if any
  - affected node
  - suggested change
  - proof check
  - risk review
  - commit readiness
  - authorization state
  - private PR creation state
  - Dave notification state

first_meaningful_suggestion: >
  Because the repo currently has no open issues or pull requests, yawn.bot
  should not infer a product thesis yet. The correct first contribution is to
  encode this feedback-to-commit gate so future feedback can be promoted from
  raw signal to thesis to risk-reviewed contribution.

proof:
  source:
    - core-loop.yawn
    - records/yawn.bot-verification-2026-07-01.yawn
    - records/yawn.bot-feedback-loop-closure-2026-09-07.yawn
    - agents/yawn.bot.yawn
    - automation/yawn.bot.daily.yawn
    - automation/yawn.bot.pr-notification.yawn
    - migrations/2026-08-17-canonical-extension.yawn
  status: seed-backed
